type: text

---

This community despises AI because it is frequently used by individuals to 'fix' problems that never existed, or by someone with no knowledge of how to maintain a codebase, let alone one run by AI agents which in turn renders entire projects untrustworthy. AI is only an acceptable tool when wielded by experienced developers who have the expertise to catch its mistakes, rigorously review the code, and make sound technical decisions. No matter how good a project's core idea might be, relying on blindly generated, unsupervised AI code instantly destroys trust in its execution.
